From 3cc195d03a8603c8e93555589fa1213f908e5125 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Leary <stephen@terriblefire.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:24:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] XC95XL: follow iMPACT's erase and program flow, stop on
 failure

- gpiod and parport cables: shift zeros on TDI when the caller gives no
  TDI data, as IOBase::shiftTDO says. tdi_byte was uninitialised, so every
  status read shifted an unknown bit into the erase/program register.
- ISP enable is ISPEN (0xE8) with 0x05, as iMPACT sends, not ISPENC
  (0xE9) with 0x15.
- Bulk erase with 0x3FFFF and read its status with 0x3FFFD; blank check
  with 0x00003, status 0x00001. Waits run at least iMPACT's TCK count and
  at least a minimum time.
- Program status is read as iMPACT does: a control 00 shift after the
  sector's control 11 word.
- Erase and program each enter and leave ISP mode.
- Read and verify shift zeros in the data field.
- A failed erase, blank check or sector stops with exit status 1 instead
  of programming or verifying anyway.
- Before touching the device, refuse a JEDEC file that does not parse,
  has the wrong fuse count, a bad checksum, or names another device.
